$ node scripts/build-web.mjs   # apps/client, dist/ already fresh, verified
$ node scripts/serve-static.mjs 8092 &
$ curl -so /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' http://localhost:8092/content/packs/es-419/books/es-fabulas-samaniego/audio/01.mp3
200
$ curl -so /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' -H 'Range: bytes=0-1' http://localhost:8092/.../01.mp3
200   # serve-static.mjs ignores Range entirely -> always 200, never 206.
       # (rules out the "Cache API rejects 206" theory as the cause here)

Playwright run against http://localhost:8092 (real static export, real sw.js,
real dist/): seeded preferences via IndexedDB (same keyval-store pattern as
screenshots.mjs), navigated to /reader/es-fabulas-samaniego?mode=narration,
waited for navigator.serviceWorker.ready, waited 4-6s for content fetches +
narration autostart, then read back every Cache Storage key.

Result: caches.keys() = ["sotto-shell-<version>"] only. NO
"sotto-content-*" cache exists at all -- not the chapter JSON, not the
audio mp3, not even the /content/packs index. Worse than Gate 1's "1 file
for this book" -- on this run it's 0 files.

Root cause (verified by listening to actual page.on('request') traffic
during the same run):

  http://localhost:8790/content/packs
  http://localhost:8790/content/packs/es-419/books/es-fabulas-samaniego/book.json
  http://localhost:8790/content/packs/es-419/books/es-fabulas-samaniego/audio/01.mp3
  http://localhost:8790/content/packs/es-419/books/es-fabulas-samaniego/chapters/01.json

Every content/audio request went to localhost:8790 (apps/server), NOT to
localhost:8092 (the static export's own origin the page was loaded from).
apps/client/src/state/contentApi.ts's serverUrl() (lines 27-34):

  export function serverUrl(): string {
    const configured = process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_SERVER_URL;
    if (configured) return configured;
    const loc = (globalThis as { location?: ... }).location;
    if (loc && !/^(localhost|127\.0\.0\.1|\[::1\])$/.test(loc.hostname)) return loc.origin;
    return 'http://localhost:8790';
  }

The comment above it says the static-hosting case ("packs are served from
the page's own origin") is detected by checking the hostname ISN'T
localhost/127.0.0.1. That heuristic is backwards for local verification of
the static build: serving the exported dist/ on localhost:8092 (exactly
what scripts/serve-static.mjs is for) makes loc.hostname === 'localhost',
so this function falls through to the hardcoded 'http://localhost:8790'
dev-server URL instead of loc.origin (8092) -- even though dist/content/
packs/** is bundled into the static export and IS being served correctly
by serve-static.mjs on 8092 (verified: the two curl checks above against
:8092 both return 200).

Combined with apps/client/public/sw.js's fetch handler (line ~94):
  if (url.origin !== self.location.origin) return; // pass through, untouched
every content request -- book.json, chapter json, AND the audio mp3 alike
-- is cross-origin relative to the page (8092 vs 8790) and the SW never
intercepts any of them, so cache-first content caching never engages for
ANY content file in this configuration, not just audio.

This means: (a) the specific "audio not cached" asymmetry Gate 1 saw is
plausibly a variant of this same bug (their setup may have had a
:8790 vs real deployed origin mismatch too, or EXPO_PUBLIC_SERVER_URL set
inconsistently), and (b) more importantly, there is currently no way to
locally verify the production static-export offline-caching path by
serving it on localhost -- it will only ever exercise the real caching
code path once deployed to a non-localhost hostname (e.g. Vercel), which
this session did not do. Not authorized to fix contentApi.ts (outside Lane
E ownership) -- reported as a finding only.
